        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "International Registrations Designating Australia (IRDA) have different requirements from standard applications in relation to registration."
        },
        {
          "depth": 1,
          "kind": "list_item",
          "text": "Part 60 The Madrid Protocol"
        },
        {
          "kind": "paragraph",
          "text": "Once an IRDA has gained protection in Australia, a notice of protection is sent to the IB and the Australian/New Zealand address for service (if one is recorded). This notice is attached to the file records, and includes the extent of the protection."
        }
